//! HTTP client backed by the browser Fetch API.
//!
//! Requests require the `Http` and `Net(host:port)` capabilities. A URL host
//! must be an ASCII hostname or a full IP address, such as `127.0.0.1`. Other
//! hosts fail with kind `"parse"`. The browser controls forbidden request
//! headers, omits ambient cookies, and enforces CORS rules on cross-origin
//! responses. Redirects fail with kind `"http"`. The browser buffers the full
//! response body before `open` returns. `max_http_body` therefore applies to
//! both `open` and `request`, and `timeout` covers the entire exchange.

import io
import json
